/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/563.json", "paragraphs": ["The bombs hit residential buildings in the southern city. More people are still missing and may be under the rubble. The acting mayor said the ground floor was hit, and the floors above collapsed.", "More than 80 workers are searching for survivors, and they stop often to listen for noises under the rubble. President Zelensky said the attack showed Russia's \"true intentions\" because it keeps attacking instead of choosing peace.", "Zelensky also criticised a deal by US President Trump that eases sanctions on Russian diesel. He called it a gift to Putin, although analysts say Trump wants to lower fuel prices before the midterm elections.", "Zaporizhzhia has more than 700,000 residents and sits less than 16km from the front line. This year, civilian casualties in Ukraine have jumped by 55%, according to the UN, as the war continues."], "paragraphs_zh": ["炸弹击中了这座南部城市的居民楼。还有人失踪，可能被埋在废墟下。代理市长说，一楼被击中，上面的楼层倒塌了。", "80多名救援人员正在搜寻生还者，他们经常停下来，听废墟下有没有声音。泽连斯基总统说，这次袭击显示了俄罗斯的“真实意图”，因为它继续攻击，而不是选择和平。", "泽连斯基还批评了美国总统特朗普的一项协议，该协议放松了对俄罗斯柴油的制裁。他称之为给普京的礼物，不过分析人士说，特朗普想在中期选举前降低燃料价格。", "扎波罗热有70多万居民，距离前线不到16公里。据联合国统计，今年乌克兰的平民伤亡人数上升了55%，战争仍在继续。"], "body": "The bombs hit residential buildings in the southern city. More people are still missing and may be under the rubble. The acting mayor said the ground floor was hit, and the floors above collapsed.\n\nMore than 80 workers are searching for survivors, and they stop often to listen for noises under the rubble. President Zelensky said the attack showed Russia's \"true intentions\" because it keeps attacking instead of choosing peace.\n\nZelensky also criticised a deal by US President Trump that eases sanctions on Russian diesel. He called it a gift to Putin, although analysts say Trump wants to lower fuel prices before the midterm elections.\n\nZaporizhzhia has more than 700,000 residents and sits less than 16km from the front line. This year, civilian casualties in Ukraine have jumped by 55%, according to the UN, as the war continues.", "body_zh": "炸弹击中了这座南部城市的居民楼。还有人失踪，可能被埋在废墟下。代理市长说，一楼被击中，上面的楼层倒塌了。\n\n80多名救援人员正在搜寻生还者，他们经常停下来，听废墟下有没有声音。泽连斯基总统说，这次袭击显示了俄罗斯的“真实意图”，因为它继续攻击，而不是选择和平。\n\n泽连斯基还批评了美国总统特朗普的一项协议，该协议放松了对俄罗斯柴油的制裁。他称之为给普京的礼物，不过分析人士说，特朗普想在中期选举前降低燃料价格。\n\n扎波罗热有70多万居民，距离前线不到16公里。据联合国统计，今年乌克兰的平民伤亡人数上升了55%，战争仍在继续。", "text": "The bombs hit residential buildings in the southern city. More people are still missing and may be under the rubble. The acting mayor said the ground floor was hit, and the floors above collapsed. More than 80 workers are searching for survivors, and they stop often to listen for noises under the rubble. President Zelensky said the attack showed Russia's \"true intentions\" because it keeps attacking instead of choosing peace. Zelensky also criticised a deal by US President Trump that eases sanctions on Russian diesel. He called it a gift to Putin, although analysts say Trump wants to lower fuel prices before the midterm elections. Zaporizhzhia has more than 700,000 residents and sits less than 16km from the front line. This year, civilian casualties in Ukraine have jumped by 55%, according to the UN, as the war continues.", "vocab": [{"word": "glide bomb", "pos": "noun", "zh": "滑翔炸弹", "note": "一种从飞机上投放、能滑翔飞行的炸弹", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "residential", "pos": "adj", "zh": "住宅的", "note": "residential buildings 指居民楼", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "rubble", "pos": "noun", "zh": "废墟；瓦砾", "note": "常与 under 连用，如 under the rubble", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "injured", "pos": "adj", "zh": "受伤的", "note": "动词是 injure", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "survivor", "pos": "noun", "zh": "生还者", "note": "动词 survive 表示幸存", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "collapse", "pos": "verb", "zh": "倒塌", "note": "过去式 collapsed", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "sanction", "pos": "noun", "zh": "制裁", "note": "常用复数 sanctions", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "ease", "pos": "verb", "zh": "放松；减轻", "note": "ease sanctions 意为放松制裁", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "civilian", "pos": "noun", "zh": "平民", "note": "civilian casualties 指平民伤亡", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "casualty", "pos": "noun", "zh": "伤亡人员", "note": "常用复数 casualties", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Russian glide bomb attack on Zaporizhzhia kills at least 20 people", "summary_original": "Volodymyr Zelensky says the attack, which left children dead, was Russia expressing its \"thanks\" for a US diesel deal.", "body_original": "Russian glide bomb attack on Zaporizhzhia kills at least 20 people\nBy\nVitaly Shevchenko\nand\nTom McArthur\nPublished\n10 October 2026\nRussia has attacked the Ukrainian city of Zaporizhzhia with five glide bombs, killing at least 20 people including four children, local officials said.\nThe glide bombs hit residential buildings in the southern city on Saturday morning. At least\n32 others were injured in the attack, with more still missing and believed to be under the rubble.\nUkrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said the attacks on Zaporizhzhia were Russia expressing \"its thanks\" for a deal announced by US President Donald Trump last night easing sanctions on Moscow to import Russian diesel.\nHe added that 13 other regions had come under attack overnight, arguing this demonstrated Russia took \"any easing of pressure to mean they can keep fighting\".\nPhotos and videos from the site of one of the strikes in Zaporizhzhia show an apartment block mostly destroyed.\n\"The ground floor was hit, and the floors above just collapsed,\" acting Mayor Regina Harchenko told Ukrainian television from the scene.\nShe said more than 80 workers were involved in ongoing search and rescue operations which are expected to continue throughout the day.\nThe rescuers regularly stop to listen for any noises made by survivors who could be under the rubble.\nHarchenko said Russia had struck at \"our very heart\" and \"our littlest ones\" were among those killed, adding that their deaths were \"awful grief for their families. For the city.\"\nZaporizhzhia is a major regional centre with more than 700,000 residents. It is located less than 10 miles (16km) from the front line\nand is frequently attacked by Russian drones and missiles\n.\nTrump announces deal for Russian diesel as Zelensky calls it a gift to Putin\nPublished\n9 hours ago\nAnalysis: Trump's shock Russia deal highlights mounting pressure to curb fuel prices\nPublished\n1 day ago\nZelensky was quick to criticise Trump's diesel deal with Russia, calling it\na gift to Russian President Vladimir Putin\n. Analysts view the deal as an attempt by the US president to allay domestic concerns about high fuel prices ahead of the upcoming midterm elections.\nZelensky wrote on social media on Saturday that Russian attacks on energy facilities in the capital, Kyiv, demonstrated Russia's \"true intentions\".\n\"Russia's choice is war. And they will be ready to end it only when they feel that their ability to drag the war out is diminishing.\n\"Unfortunately, the signals Russia received yesterday were entirely different – signals suggesting that it could simply keep attacking. And this needs to be corrected.\"\nBoth Russia and Ukraine have stepped up attacks on infrastructure in recent months, as Moscow's full-scale invasion, launched in 2022, drags on.\nOn Thursday, at least 33 people were killed in another Russian glide bomb attack on two civilian buses in Kramatorsk, in the eastern Donetsk region.\nThe day before,\n22 people including five children\ndied as a Russian missile hit an apartment block in the town of Pryluky, east of Kyiv.\nThe number of civilian casualties in Ukraine\njumped by 55%\n,\nexternal\nin the first eight months of this year, according to the UN.\nRussia has\nalso stepped up its attacks on Ukrainian energy infrastructure\nas winter approaches, a strategy it has undertaken in previous years. Kyiv has repeatedly accused it of targeting Ukraine's civilian population, which Moscow denies.\nFor its part, Ukraine has increasingly adopted a policy of striking infrastructure often deep inside Russia that is crucial to its economy, including several oil refineries and terminals.\nSeveral\nstrikes on data centres owned by Yandex\nhave left the tech giant struggling to maintain services.\nKyiv says its strikes are aimed at curtailing revenue streams for Russia's war machine.\nRelated topics\nWar in Ukraine\nUkraine\nMore on this story\nWatch: Fleeing Kyiv for the countryside ahead of winter\nPublished\n1 day ago\nFear and disruption for Ukraine's rail passengers as Russia escalates drone attacks\nPublished\n4 days ago\nRussia targeting 'ordinary life' with attacks on Ukraine's data centres, Zelensky says\nPublished\n25 September", "fetched_at": "2026-10-11T00:25:09.061571", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.263, "sm": 100, "em": 262, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "bombs", "s": 0.275, "e": 0.663, "sm": 275, "em": 662, "cs": 4, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "hit", "s": 0.675, "e": 0.888, "sm": 675, "em": 887, "cs": 10, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "residential", "s": 0.9, "e": 1.513, "sm": 900, "em": 1512, "cs": 14, "ce": 25, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "buildings", "s": 1.525, "e": 1.987, "sm": 1525, "em": 1987, "cs": 26, "ce": 35, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "in", "s": 2.0, "e": 2.087, "sm": 2000, "em": 2087, "cs": 36, "ce": 38, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "the", "s": 2.1, "e": 2.188, "sm": 2100, "em": 2187, "cs": 39, "ce": 42, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "southern", "s": 2.2, "e": 2.562, "sm": 2200, "em": 2562, "cs": 43, "ce": 51, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "city", "s": 2.575, "e": 2.988, "sm": 2575, "em": 2987, "cs": 52, "ce": 56, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": ".", "s": 2.988, "e": 3.85, "sm": 2987, "em": 3850, "cs": 56, "ce": 57, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "More", "s": 3.85, "e": 4.138, "sm": 3850, "em": 4137, "cs": 58, "ce": 62, "si": 1}, {"i": 11, "w": "people", "s": 4.15, "e": 4.5, "sm": 4150, "em": 4500, "c